#EXTM3U
# Internet radio for evo-esp32: copy this folder to the card and the
# stations appear in the library under Radio. Each #EXTINF line names
# the station on the URL line below it; tvg-logo="..." is its picture
# (a URL, or a path on the card relative to this file). Add or remove
# as you like, or put your own .m3u or .pls files here.
#
# A selection of UK stations, and Radio Paradise's two FLAC streams
# from the US, drawn from the radio-browser.info directory and checked
# on 20 October 2026: every stream answered, every logo decoded. The
# streams and logos are the broadcasters' own. What this player decodes
# from the air: MP3, FLAC and Ogg Vorbis. AAC streams (Absolute, Planet
# Rock, Kerrang!, Greatest Hits and the other Bauer brands) are not
# played on the ESP32-C5 board; the BBC's live streams are HLS, which
# no evo-esp32 plays yet.

